[ceiling] Ten functional flat M5 screw-head bearings. The Ø8.5 × 5 mm socket heads require these Z5.4 mm planes; each pocket opens through the casing wall for its driver and support removal. The actual Normal(auto)/Snug slice has exactly ten short support bodies, all below Z5.03 mm and in these open mouths, with 21.019 mm minimum full-bead bed margin. Remove them outward before hardware and foil. See cold-core/foam-shell/printability-review.json for their individual footprints. Physical release force is not established by this access reading.
alternatives: Tapering the bearing replaces the head's flat load surface. Opening it upward removes the screw-head bearing. Automatic Tree(auto)/Default trials, including zero extra support-foot flange, cross this wide cap's required 20 mm bed border; the compact normal choice is scoped to these ten pockets.
